provider_responses.text:
The key next step is to balance **psychological safety, accountability, and practical limits**.

A healthy team should:

- surface risks early without fear of humiliation;
- use clear facts and ownership to solve problems;
- address repeated negligence or misconduct directly;
- avoid turning every setback into bureaucracy or a group discussion;
- recognize when the real issue is inadequate time, staffing, authority, or scope.

The best test is not whether the team seems calm or positive. It is whether people can tell the truth early, make decisions clearly, adapt when reality changes, and still be held to meaningful standards.

